# mlmf-gguf parses bytes.
#
# `borrow` and `collections` were added when the tensor directory landed,
# and both are forced by the seam rather than chosen. `TensorContainer::
# tensor_bytes` returns `Cow<'_, [u8]>` -- mlmf-core's signature, not this
# crate's -- so `std::borrow::Cow` cannot be avoided while implementing it.
# `TensorContainer::tensor`'s own doc requires a format crate parsing a real
# model to replace the default linear scan with an index, and a HashMap is
# that index. Neither reaches outside the process, which is what C3 exists
# to forbid.
borrow
cmp
collections
error
fmt
iter
option
primitive
result
slice
str
string
sync
u32
u64
usize
vec
